/validate]} {:db/id "q-37996" :question/id #uuid "9c5423a0-a399-5841-a575-289a1476314b" :question/math-academy-id "q-37996" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{y}(1-xy)\\,dx\\,dy=$" :question/worked-solution "The integral is defined over a type II region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{y}(1-xy)\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{y}(1-xy)\\,dx]\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[x-\\frac{y{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{{y}^{2}}^{y}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{2}-({y}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{5}}{2}))\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{2}-{y}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{5}}{2})\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{2}-{y}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{5}}{2})\\,dy & ={[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{4}}{8}-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{6}}{12}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{8}-\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{12}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-37996/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fdce40e5-8ffe-52cb-8a8e-ac8eaea982f0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-37996"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132421/selection/5a1fe28b022029f27455dc36a9cc0dbfd0eced1186649091706824f56db6ba8d" :answer/id #uuid "6c759950-3a42-51cc-993b-ab64b895ecc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132421/selection/1365a3b13f0ed1122052c11776d4286702b89cd082eec9cdd1b43f23075c8eaa" :answer/id #uuid "d78e9ee2-047b-5e89-b606-60fc204aadad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+\\frac{1}{e}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132421/selection/d67855e465bb8b60e3c344317c16f58fe46efd485b13d5dd335c01e7334c43ce" :answer/id #uuid "58103bfa-a285-51e1-a2be-f5e7c605dc15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e-\\frac{1}{e}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132421/selection/7b1af5d56d15677521357cd2c3dd23a89bd88ae93e2476937f6fb7888002961a" :answer/id #uuid "3fe6c62d-6e38-58fd-b085-86453a09e5bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{e}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132421/selection/ace37c2040207cebb14b55c05840a4c383db24d63f2349cf49f8db6a85f5faeb" :answer/id #uuid "9964b396-9653-52ce-9579-6cadd757d39b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132421/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "26965548-0d00-5094-aca1-d03a9c036f40" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132421/selection/d67855e465bb8b60e3c344317c16f58fe46efd485b13d5dd335c01e7334c43ce" :answer-field/choices ["q-132421/selection/5a1fe28b022029f27455dc36a9cc0dbfd0eced1186649091706824f56db6ba8d" "q-132421/selection/1365a3b13f0ed1122052c11776d4286702b89cd082eec9cdd1b43f23075c8eaa" "q-132421/selection/d67855e465bb8b60e3c344317c16f58fe46efd485b13d5dd335c01e7334c43ce" "q-132421/selection/7b1af5d56d15677521357cd2c3dd23a89bd88ae93e2476937f6fb7888002961a" "q-132421/selection/ace37c2040207cebb14b55c05840a4c383db24d63f2349cf49f8db6a85f5faeb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132421" :question/id #uuid "30f6dbff-f649-5725-b4bd-0bb3cfdf4187" :question/math-academy-id "q-132421" :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}\\,dx\\,dy.$" :question/worked-solution "The integral is defined over a type II region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}[x]_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-0)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}\\,dy & =[-{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}]_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi }-(-{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡0}) \\\\  & =-{e}^{-1}+{e}^{1} \\\\  & =e-\\frac{1}{e}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-132421/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fdce40e5-8ffe-52cb-8a8e-ac8eaea982f0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132421"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81320/selection/c53fda742d514dd498dc2a3065d035257b7cfc54103a9f93cd46b054f212d1b5" :answer/id #uuid "e5700389-74d9-5655-b605-a75ce4a0605e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{27}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81320/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer/id #uuid "ef4ba8e8-1655-50a5-b4ec-735d385a1916" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81320/selection/2b24e8943a06d1441f9205f893f528009e371bc76b428bc2428e041586b5f6ef" :answer/id #uuid "f483089b-1921-5111-9b82-95093ed6819e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81320/selection/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" :answer/id #uuid "7dd5e7bc-235d-5975-a02f-c1d5b119bb5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81320/selection/7627fb02fec1c7a865cb3e7797f7ea7835cb8ec3423f266885f8f5d01084e358" :answer/id #uuid "62fcadbd-bd99-5c73-a2b5-702e5c087370" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81320/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9757dc81-7980-5f3f-a73c-c2a54ef6fbbf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81320/selection/c53fda742d514dd498dc2a3065d035257b7cfc54103a9f93cd46b054f212d1b5" :answer-field/choices ["q-81320/selection/c53fda742d514dd498dc2a3065d035257b7cfc54103a9f93cd46b054f212d1b5" "q-81320/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" "q-81320/selection/2b24e8943a06d1441f9205f893f528009e371bc76b428bc2428e041586b5f6ef" "q-81320/selection/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" "q-81320/selection/7627fb02fec1c7a865cb3e7797f7ea7835cb8ec3423f266885f8f5d01084e358"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81320" :question/id #uuid "67b5ec5f-9e3b-51f6-93fe-06568326e407" :question/math-academy-id "q-81320" :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{1}^{{y}^{3}}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,dx\\,dy.$" :question/worked-solution "The integral is defined over a type II region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{1}^{{y}^{3}}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}[{\\int }_{1}^{{y}^{3}}dx]\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}[x]_{1}^{{y}^{3}}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}({y}^{3}-1)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}(y-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}})\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}(y-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}})\\,dy & ={[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{1}{y}]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =(8+\\frac{1}{4})-(\\frac{1}{2}+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-81320/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fdce40e5-8ffe-52cb-8a8e-ac8eaea982f0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81320"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81309/selection/c5088eba57e2ccad1c142c648ad8fc84409c72cc9a171be8634327f163ebc3be" :answer/id #uuid "a1eaf375-494b-5fad-8cee-15762116cdac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81309/selection/0df7b38feee6b329728a75385b5ac5cf692617d021d8d1df886374cb2953e307" :answer/id #uuid "3c11b4dc-13bd-511e-8f5f-7b447c4ebe7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81309/selection/e72c45ace96097f93f383a573acb0537fd6df30025f9556bb543356dcc9c34a0" :answer/id #uuid "182210cf-2659-565a-9f73-2a12d001e499" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1)-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81309/selection/f37ded3c0d8983c69cac3cab2b38c94b188fc85612906e5997896ede23c9ef0d" :answer/id #uuid "f1c78e7a-8b16-538d-96a2-da00844af13f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81309/selection/ae28e38e663c6924bbe365ac585b2e32772dd7aaf9c7c0952e104354f367de3a" :answer/id #uuid "34b04a54-facd-5181-be17-e6881fede358" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1)+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81309/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6ad702c6-d355-5943-9183-a343509e57b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81309/selection/e72c45ace96097f93f383a573acb0537fd6df30025f9556bb543356dcc9c34a0" :answer-field/choices ["q-81309/selection/c5088eba57e2ccad1c142c648ad8fc84409c72cc9a171be8634327f163ebc3be" "q-81309/selection/0df7b38feee6b329728a75385b5ac5cf692617d021d8d1df886374cb2953e307" "q-81309/selection/e72c45ace96097f93f383a573acb0537fd6df30025f9556bb543356dcc9c34a0" "q-81309/selection/f37ded3c0d8983c69cac3cab2b38c94b188fc85612906e5997896ede23c9ef0d" "q-81309/selection/ae28e38e663c6924bbe365ac585b2e32772dd7aaf9c7c0952e104354f367de3a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81309" :question/id #uuid "6c391d3b-2ef4-5185-8c90-e28518247763" :question/math-academy-id "q-81309" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y-1}^{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,dx\\,dy=$" :question/worked-solution "The integral is defined over a type II region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y-1}^{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{y-1}^{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,dx]\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]_{y-1}^{0}\\,dy \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡0-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y-1))\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y-1)-1)\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y-1)-1)\\,dy & =[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y-1)-y]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)-1)-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-1)-0) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1)-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-81309/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fdce40e5-8ffe-52cb-8a8e-ac8eaea982f0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81309"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132562/selection/29e18d29d5a8d00489a807deb821c9d8fb2c816d74392c4ec1d541f26b369225" :answer/id #uuid "2758e88f-d1df-5ec6-840f-df02d615ad30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132562/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" :answer/id #uuid "392ea7d1-3a92-5a9f-b538-070778a2527b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132562/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "cac34dfe-54b3-5c46-9881-eaa692a22f2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132562/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "3d8dc75d-93a5-5526-97b2-4b22a8aefdf0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132562/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "cef645cc-499c-57d9-9907-f7d9e4df8858" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132562/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c32b5e54-42da-531c-b5b3-821a6d967b9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132562/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer-field/choices ["q-132562/selection/29e18d29d5a8d00489a807deb821c9d8fb2c816d74392c4ec1d541f26b369225" "q-132562/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" "q-132562/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-132562/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-132562/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132562" :question/id #uuid "4f1f896d-423d-5f07-bb8f-0a0deac07744" :question/math-academy-id "q-132562" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14055472/assets/d5f54020da277980a58151bf2a85911365e67ecae6832881e03ac8b9b6431e6a.png)\n\nEvaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}4x\\,dA,\\,$\nwhere $D$ is the region enclosed between the curves $16{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16$ and $4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16,$ above the $x$-axis, as shown in the picture." :question/worked-solution "Notice that $D$ is a type II region. Since $x\\ge 0,$ we obtain the following equations in terms of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16 & \\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}} \\\\ 4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16 & \\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{4-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits of integration.\n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}} & =\\sqrt{4-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}} \\\\ 1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & =4-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} \\\\ \\frac{3}{16}{y}^{2} & =3 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =16 \\\\ y & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince our region lies above the $x$-axis, the $y$-limits are \n$0\\le y\\le 4.$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14055472/assets/d8b8b05e9004f6b25f635e9c39421a8e8e27831a26a22273cf88572df89ffc45.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 4,\\,\\sqrt{1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{4-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}4x\\,dA={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}/16}}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}/4}}\\,4x\\,dx\\,dy\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}/16}}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}/4}}\\,4x\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}2[{\\int }_{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}/16}}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}/4}}\\,2x\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\,2{[\\,{x}^{2}\\,]}_{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}/16}}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}/4}}\\text{ }dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\,2[4-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-(1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16})]dy \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\,[3-\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{2}]dy \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\,(1-\\frac{1}{16}{y}^{2})dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\,(1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16})dy & =6{[y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{48}]}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =6(4-\\frac{64}{48}) \\\\  & =6(4-\\frac{4}{3}) \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{8}{3} \\\\  & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-132562/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90f7718f-e014-5232-acb1-6773ab79f61d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132562"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132527/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" :answer/id #uuid "327c164b-7f45-55af-b466-bc9ff6cf052a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132527/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "9ffd597e-f8d4-5ec2-93f1-0a20dab32d11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132527/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "f6281426-a22c-56a4-b7cd-d229021e250e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132527/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "444fac14-f20e-5218-b051-c8c326242701" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132527/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "d0d14262-dd20-5cfa-a9f8-6b9a9a7ad393" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132527/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0e9b8828-4a18-5a98-a51e-db91abf63004" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132527/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer-field/choices ["q-132527/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" "q-132527/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-132527/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-132527/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-132527/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132527" :question/id #uuid "1c5ca9ca-aaf0-57a5-9113-ae2d9b07398d" :question/math-academy-id "q-132527" :question/problem "Calculate ${∬}_{D}y\\,dA,$ where $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,2{y}^{2}\\le x\\le {y}^{2}+1}.$" :question/worked-solution "The integral is defined over a type II region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,2{y}^{2}\\le x\\le {y}^{2}+1}.$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}y\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2{y}^{2}}^{{y}^{2}+1}y\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2{y}^{2}}^{{y}^{2}+1}y\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y[{\\int }_{2{y}^{2}}^{{y}^{2}+1}\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y[\\,x\\,]_{2{y}^{2}}^{{y}^{2}+1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y({y}^{2}+1-2{y}^{2})dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(y-{y}^{3})\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(y-{y}^{3})\\,dy & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-132527/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90f7718f-e014-5232-acb1-6773ab79f61d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132527"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81395/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "37864aa5-0f9a-5c72-93f5-f3617cc715fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81395/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer/id #uuid "7bda23f6-6f68-5d9a-a1e0-47e23b7213d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81395/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "1bcc51c7-00d7-5b95-90a0-8fceb7dcfad7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81395/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "8f2366f8-c2e9-5fb9-8bdd-90084f93725f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81395/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" :answer/id #uuid "41d4a459-68c0-53ce-80c8-e512dcb0f122" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81395/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8549113f-232a-5575-8e07-f9e818e96622" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81395/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-81395/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-81395/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" "q-81395/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" "q-81395/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-81395/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81395" :question/id #uuid "9e6f245d-e90c-5a95-8ef4-6c1feb736768" :question/math-academy-id "q-81395" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14055472/assets/ff3b9f52ed01d991d1fff18e78c494488b53703669b6bb326b5436a19c952a18.png)\n\nEvaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}x\\,dA,\\,$\nwhere $D$ is the region enclosed between the curves $3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=9$ and ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=9,$ as shown in the picture." :question/worked-solution "Notice that $D$ is a type II region. Since $x\\ge 0,$ we obtain the following equations in terms of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=9 & \\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}} \\\\ 3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=9 & \\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{3-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits of integration.\n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{3-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}} \\\\ 9-{y}^{2} & =3-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}{y}^{2} & =6 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, since our region lies above the line the $x$-axis, the $y$-limits are \n$0\\le y\\le 3.$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14055472/assets/91f377562a1e94218b7be886cd63638e8881b0c4fac231a810bb6bff3a1fe643.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\sqrt{3-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}x\\,dA={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{3-{y}^{2}/3}}^{\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}}x\\,dx\\,dy\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{3-{y}^{2}/3}}^{\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}}x\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{\\sqrt{3-{y}^{2}/3}}^{\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}}x\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{\\sqrt{3-{y}^{2}/3}}^{\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{2}(9-{y}^{2}-(3-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}))\\,dy \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(6-\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{2})\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(6-\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{2})\\,dy & =\\frac{1}{2}{[6y-\\frac{2}{9}{y}^{3}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(18-6-0) \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-81395/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90f7718f-e014-5232-acb1-6773ab79f61d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81395"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-40680/selection/d427b944e26709d5f365fc6b5711be004a0a3509f614cbfd4943dc70d3f6d84e" :answer/id #uuid "d9c26741-e06a-5a76-89c3-e1aa628250dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40680/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "d6a5ee6b-62ea-5ce5-99fe-49fd2bc7e5ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40680/selection/2b998a440c758092569557828849b9a2d05282247ea8a11a5727b6cadcbcb080" :answer/id #uuid "1831ae25-1d51-5418-8e56-316433b45b16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40680/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "d650f2a8-2f5e-5d66-980b-531f0c04b5b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40680/selection/a272cbe64fea514fe5c8c9685aef2c9378fdfe44c54941c8bcba64a5f713bc84" :answer/id #uuid "ce67e1ef-dcbb-5755-8ed4-51bdcb66eda3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40680/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "02ba99cd-cd32-5955-8db9-be3261dc6513" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-40680/selection/a272cbe64fea514fe5c8c9685aef2c9378fdfe44c54941c8bcba64a5f713bc84" :answer-field/choices ["q-40680/selection/d427b944e26709d5f365fc6b5711be004a0a3509f614cbfd4943dc70d3f6d84e" "q-40680/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" "q-40680/selection/2b998a440c758092569557828849b9a2d05282247ea8a11a5727b6cadcbcb080" "q-40680/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-40680/selection/a272cbe64fea514fe5c8c9685aef2c9378fdfe44c54941c8bcba64a5f713bc84"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-40680" :question/id #uuid "7a5b3321-cf12-51db-a631-dd5473f67f10" :question/math-academy-id "q-40680" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14055472/assets/a135b0766239bcd6e9cacc324572486e66e1c859ecd28a4d59ef7795cc511ed4.png)\n\nEvaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}xy\\,dA,\\,$\nwhere $D$ is the region enclosed between the curves ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4$ and $x=0,$ above the $x$-axis and below the line $y=1,$ as shown in the picture." :question/worked-solution "Notice that $D$ is a type II region. Since $x\\ge 0,$ we obtain the following equations in terms of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4 & \\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}} \\\\ x=0 & \\,⟹\\,x=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits of integration.\n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}} & =0 \\\\ 4-{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, since our region lies above the $x$-axis and below the line $y=1,$ the $y$-limits are \n$0\\le y\\le 1.$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14055472/assets/373286c03cc595535a7f04987e7454be2fac547d769341343f05ea67ee0b001d.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}xy\\,dA={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}\\,xy\\,dx\\,dy\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}\\,xy\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}\\,xy\\,dx]\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,{[\\,\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}y\\,]}_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}\\text{ }dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\frac{1}{2}(4-{y}^{2})ydy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\frac{1}{2}(4y-{y}^{3})dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\frac{1}{2}(4y-{y}^{3})dy & ={[\\frac{1}{2}(2{y}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4})]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2-\\frac{1}{4})-\\frac{1}{2}(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-40680/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90f7718f-e014-5232-acb1-6773ab79f61d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40680"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132531/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "cdcaecb2-46b2-5639-ba48-d4c2a6a4feb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132531/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "563a7936-6784-57ac-87a6-ba67f7c55bde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132531/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "ae1521a1-2e01-5da1-972d-4a0cf33595a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132531/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "51ba1e79-03e1-55ed-9700-630c49339e1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132531/selection/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf" :answer/id #uuid "17b234b1-8ffc-5360-9b5e-785ffd382aee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132531/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ae60d52d-9b12-5be9-bf60-0895f7fb9630" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132531/selection/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf" :answer-field/choices ["q-132531/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-132531/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-132531/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-132531/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-132531/selection/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132531" :question/id #uuid "b686fe8e-540c-5e6e-855f-cc2825f800a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-132531" :question/problem "Calculate ${∬}_{D}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}\\,dA,$ where $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le x\\le {y}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "The integral is defined over a type II region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le x\\le {y}^{2}}.$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{y}[{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}{x}^{2}\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{y}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{y}(\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{6}-0)dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{5}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{5}\\,dy & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{5}\\,dy \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[\\frac{1}{6}{y}^{6}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{32}{3}-\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{21}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-132531/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90f7718f-e014-5232-acb1-6773ab79f61d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132531"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7134"] :question/problem "If $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the curves $y=\\sqrt{x-2}$ and $y=1-x$ from $y=0$ to $y=1,$ as shown below, then what is $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_D (x^2y+xy^2) \\, \\mathrm{d}A$ expressed as a repeated integral?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14055472/assets/0e4cf57408f9ca18dc4613317b8b9bc8b3149da0bf273ad03a8a8a48a6e6f454.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, let's represent $D$ as a type II region. Writing $y=\\sqrt{x-2}$ and $y=1-x$ in terms of $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=\\sqrt{x-2} & \\,⟹\\,x={y}^{2}+2 \\\\ y=1-x & \\,⟹\\,x=1-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14055472/assets/f0e531c612c84aa0260b318aa1fbe21c9089270b8c4a1079e08583b7fc5a5d90.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD = \\bigg\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1, \\quad 1-y \\leq x  \\leq y^2+2 \\bigg\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}({x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2})\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-y}^{{y}^{2}+2}({x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2})\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7135"] :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed between the curves $y=x^2$ and $y=3-2x$ below the line $y=3.$ What is $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} f\\left( {x,y} \\right) \\, \\mathrm{d}A\\:$ expressed as a repeated integral?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make a sketch of our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14055472/assets/ffbe0db1ae1bb082e63b0d97324b43dd78334dfbd1e88aaa0744be039dd0efc6.png)\n\nWe need to represent $D$ as a type II region. Writing $y=x^2$ and $y=3-2x$ in terms of $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y={x}^{2} & \\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{y} \\\\ y=3-2x & \\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{3-y}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits of integration.\n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{y} & =\\frac{3-y}{2} \\\\ 4y & =(3-y)^{2} \\\\ 4y & =9-6y+{y}^{2} \\\\ {y}^{2}-10y+9 & =0 \\\\ (y-1)(y-9) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, since our region lies below the line $y=3,$ the $y$-limits are \n\n$$\n1 \\le y \\le 3.\n$$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14055472/assets/3c56798a33ee2da6d928174b67546945be4bf3594d15e89f3ca39119dd4e2c62.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 1 \\leq y \\leq 3, \\quad \\dfrac{3-y}{2} \\leq x  \\leq \\sqrt{y} \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{(3-y)/2}^{\\sqrt{y}}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7136"] :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_{\\sqrt{\\pi}}^{\\sqrt{2\\pi}} \\int_0^{y^2} \\frac{\\sin y^2}{y} \\, \\mathrm{d}x \\,\\mathrm{d}y.$" :question/worked-solution "The integral is defined over a type II region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi }}^{\\sqrt{2\\pi }}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{2}}{y}\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi }}^{\\sqrt{2\\pi }}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{2}}{y}[{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}dx]\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi }}^{\\sqrt{2\\pi }}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{2}}{y}[x]_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi }}^{\\sqrt{2\\pi }}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{2}}{y}({y}^{2}-0)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi }}^{\\sqrt{2\\pi }}y\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{2}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi }}^{\\sqrt{2\\pi }}y\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{2}\\,dy & ={[-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{y}^{2}]}_{\\sqrt{\\pi }}^{\\sqrt{2\\pi }} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7137"] :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint \\limits_{D} xy^2\\,\\mathrm{d}A,\\:$\nwhere $D$ is the region enclosed between the curves $x^2+y^2=4$ and $x=0,$ and above the line $y=-1,$ as shown in the picture.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14055472/assets/f93aeee59ad97fde0efceff342e32a19062187261abec865616bfa963f1084a6.png)" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $D$ is a type II region. Since $x \\ge 0,$ we obtain the following equations in terms of $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4 & \\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}} \\\\ x=0 & \\,⟹\\,x=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits of integration.\n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}} & =0 \\\\ 4-{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, since our region lies above the line $y=-1,$ the $y$-limits are \n$-1 \\le y \\le 2.$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14055472/assets/8d77e3caa18191710e056b72ea54e5820e6244d9e90719222deed409d3992c5b.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: -1 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\quad 0 \\leq x  \\leq \\sqrt{4-y^2} \\right\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\iint \\limits_{D} xy^2\\,\\mathrm{d}A = \\int_{-1}^2 \\int_0^{\\sqrt{4-y^2}}\\, xy^2\\, \\mathrm dx\\,   \\mathrm{d}  y\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}\\,x{y}^{2}\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{y}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}x\\,dx]\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{y}^{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}(4-{y}^{2}-0)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}(2{y}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{4}}{2})\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(2{y}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{4}}{2})\\,dy & ={[\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}-\\frac{{y}^{5}}{10}]}_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{16}{3}-\\frac{32}{10})-(-\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{1}{10}) \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
